content.text:
The root cause is a single fault: the geo service's pod is crash-looping and never becomes ready, so search's calls to geo fail, and the failure reaches users through frontend's `/hotels` path. Everything else in the survey (rate, reservation, profile span drops) follows from the hotel flow stopping after search fails, so I found no second fault.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, count(*) n, min(value) vmin, max(value) vmax FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'geo-85ff%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.restarts','k8s.container.ready') GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Geo pod restarts climb from 3 to 6 while container ready stays 0 through the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, count(*) n, min(value) vmin, max(value) vmax FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name='geo' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Geo deployment available replicas are 0 for every sample in the abnormal window; normal was 1."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='geo' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Geo emits no server spans at all in the abnormal window, versus 1161 in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code NOT IN ('Unset','OK') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) nonok, round(avg(duration)/1e6,3) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Search's geo.Geo/Nearby client calls: 1133 of 1137 fail, averaging 0.02 ms, consistent with connection refused."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "geo", "to": "search",
     "evidence": [
       {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, substr(message,1,80) msg, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='search' AND level='ERROR' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Search logs 1533 ERRORs 'Failed to get nearby hotels from geo service' in the abnormal window."}
     ]},
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code NOT IN ('Unset','OK') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) nonok FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Frontend HTTP /hotels server spans: 1099 of 1103 non-OK, versus zero failures in normal."}
     ]}
  ]
}
```

